          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em comma category
            of two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : C \to E
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : D \to E
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            like an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} arrow category
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            where all arrows have their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/source"} source
            in the image of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            and their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target"} target
            in the image of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            (and the morphisms between arrows keep track of how these sources and targets are in these images). It can also be seen a kind of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-limit"} 2-limit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+homotopy+theory"} directed
            refinement of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            of two functors between
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p We discuss three equivalent definitions of comma categories
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#InComponents"} Explicitly in components
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#AsAPullback"} As a pullback
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#AsA2Limit"} As a 2-limit
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              The terminology “comma category” is a holdover from the original notation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f,g)
              for such a category, which generalises
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,y)
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(x,y)
              for a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f/g)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f\downarrow g)
          %h3#InComponents Via components: the objectwise definition
          %p
          #CommaCategory.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon C\to E
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \colon D\to E
              are
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
              %strong comma category
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f/g)
              whose
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triples"} triples
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi d
                        %mo ,
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (c,d,\alpha)
                  where
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi c
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c\in C
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi D
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d\in D
                #eq:MorphismMakingAnObjectInTheComma.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\alpha \colon f(c) \to g(d)
                %p
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                  in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi E
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %p and whose
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (c_1,d_1,\alpha_1)
                to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (c_2,d_2,\alpha_2)
                are pairs
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi β
                        %mo ,
                        %mi γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\beta,\gamma)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta:c_1\to c_2
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi γ
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma:d_1\to d_2
                are morphisms in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mn 2
                        %mo .
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi β
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo .
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_2 . f(\beta) = g(\gamma) . \alpha_1
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi β
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi α
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi α
                                  %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi g
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi γ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi α
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi β
                                %mo ,
                                %mi γ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mn 2
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mn 2
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi α
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    f(c_1)
                    \&amp;\stackrel{f(\beta)}{\rightarrow}&amp;
                    f(c_2)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\alpha_1}
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{\alpha_2}
                    \\\
                    g(d_1)
                    \&amp;\stackrel{g(\gamma)}{\to}&amp;
                    g(d_2)
                    \\\
                    \\\
                    (c_1,d_1, \alpha_1)
                    \&amp;\stackrel{(\beta,\gamma)}{\to}&amp;
                    (c_2,d_2, \alpha_2)
                    }
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                of morphisms is given on components by composition in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %p
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              In addition, there are two canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functors"} forgetful functors
              defined on the comma category:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  there is a functor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi H
                          %mi C
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_C\colon (f/g)\rightarrow C
                  which sends each object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi d
                        %mo ,
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (c,d,\alpha)
                  to
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi c
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi β
                        %mo ,
                        %mi γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\beta,\gamma)
                  to
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi β
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
              %li
                %p
                  there is a functor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi H
                          %mi D
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_D\colon (f/g)\rightarrow D
                  which sends each object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi d
                        %mo ,
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (c,d,\alpha)
                  to
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi β
                        %mo ,
                        %mi γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\beta,\gamma)
                  to
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi γ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            %p Furthermore:
            %ul
              %li
                there is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi θ
                      %mo :
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi g
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta : f \circ H_C \to g\circ H_D
                defined by
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi θ
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo ,
                            %mi d
                            %mo ,
                            %mi α
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi α
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_{(c,d,\alpha)} = \alpha
            %p
              These functors and natural transformation together give the comma category a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category+theory"} 2-category theoretic
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              %a{:href => "#AsA2Limit"} this section
              for more.
          %p
          #IsoCommaCategory.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              Alternatively, requiring the morphisms
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:MorphismMakingAnObjectInTheComma"} (1)
              to be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
              yields the notion of an
              %strong iso-comma category
              (an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/iso-comma+object"} iso-comma object
              in
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of a non-lax “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-pullback"}> 2-pullback
              ”.
          %h3#AsAPullback As a pullback in the 1-category of categories
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I = \{a \to b\}
            be the (directed)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+category"} interval category
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mi I
                  %mo =
                  %mi Funct
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi I
                  %mo ,
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^I = Funct(I,E)
            the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
          %p
            The comma category is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi E
                            %mi I
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "1"}
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi pb
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mo
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi F
                                    %mo ↦
                                    %mi F
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi a
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mo ×
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi F
                                    %mo ↦
                                    %mi F
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi b
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo ×
                          %mi D
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mi f
                              %mo ×
                              %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mi E
                          %mo ×
                          %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  (f/g)
                  \&amp;\to&amp;
                  E^I
                  \\\
                  \\big\downarrow
                  \&amp; \scriptsize{(pb)} &amp;
                  \\big\downarrow
                  \\mathrlap{^{\mathrlap{(F\mapsto F(a))\times(F\mapsto F(b))}}}
                  \\\
                  C \times D
                  \&amp;
                  \\underset{f \times g}{\longrightarrow}
                  \&amp;
                  E \times E
                  }
          %p
            in the standard sense of pullback of morphisms in the 1-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            of categories.
          %p
            Compare this with the construction of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            (
            %a{:href => "homotopy+pullback#HomotopyPullbackByFactorizationLemma"}> here
            ), hence with the definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} loop space object
            and also with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+universal+bundle"} generalized universal bundle
          %h3#AsA2Limit As a 2-limit in the 2-category of categories
          %p
            The comma category is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+object"} comma object
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cospan"} cospan
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi E
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mi g
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\overset{f}{\rightarrow}E\overset{g}{\leftarrow}D
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted
            2-categorical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-limit"} limit
            (in fact, a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-limit"} strict 2-limit
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi f
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi D
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; C
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^f
                  \\\
                  D &amp;\stackrel{g}{\to}&amp; E
                  }
          %p
            Specifically, it is the universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
            making the following square commute up to a specified
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
            (such a universal square is in general called a
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+square"} comma square
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi H
                                %mi C
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi H
                                    %mi D
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇙
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi f
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi D
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  (f/g) &amp;\overset{H_C}{\to}&amp; C
                  \\\
                  \\mathllap{{}^{H_D}} \downarrow &amp;\swArrow&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                  \\\
                  D &amp;\stackrel{g}{\to}&amp; E
                  }
          %p
            (Sometimes this is called a “lax pullback”, but that terminology properly refers to something else; see
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+object"} comma object
            and
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-limit"} 2-limit
          %p
            Notably, the forgetful functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_D
            from the “objectwise” definition are thus recovered via a categorical construction: they are the projections from the summit of the “appropriate” 2-categorical limit.
          %p
            In terms of the imagery of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+objects"} loop space objects
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+object"} directed paths
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            which start in the image of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            and end in the image of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
                are both the identity functor of a category
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f/g)
                is the category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C ^{\mathbf{2}}
                of arrows in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                is the identity functor of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
                is the inclusion
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\to C
                of an object
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c\in C
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f/g)
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+category"} slice category
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/c
            %li
              %p
                Likewise if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
                is the identity and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                is the inclusion of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f/g)
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/under+category"} coslice category
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c/C
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi τ
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi F
                      %mo →
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau \colon F \to G
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ,
                      %mi G
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F,G :\colon C\to D
                may be regarded as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \colon C\to (F/G)
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi τ
                        %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(c)=(c,c,\tau_c)
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(f)=(f,f)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                such that the two projections from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (F/G)
                back to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                are both
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+inverses"} left inverses
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                yields a corresponding natural transformation. This is an expression of the universal property of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (F/G)
                as a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+object"} comma object
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#completeness_and_cocompleteness Completeness and cocompleteness
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete+category"} cocomplete
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: C \to E
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocontinuous+functor"} cocontinuous
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g: D \to E
            is an arbitrary functor (not necessarily cocontinuous) then the comma category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f/g)
            is cocomplete. Similarly, as
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi g
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo ≅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mi op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mi op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f/g)^{op}\cong (g^{op}/f^{op})
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+category"} complete
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g: D \to E
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functor"} continuous
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: C \to E
            is an arbitrary functor (not necessarily continuous) then the comma category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f/g)
            is complete.
          %p For a proof, see
          %ul
            %li Rydeheard, David E., and Rod M. Burstall. Computational category theory. Vol. 152. Englewood Cliffs: Prentice Hall, 1988. Section 5.2: colimits in comma categories.
